  "response": "To configure LlamaIndex to use a local Ollama LLM and a Hugging Face embedding model globally, ensuring that OpenAI is never contacted, you can follow these steps. The context provides specific instructions and code snippets for setting up local models in LlamaIndex.\n\n1. **Set up the Local Ollama LLM**: Use the `Ollama` class from `llama_index.llms.ollama` to specify a local Ollama model. Ensure Ollama is installed and running.\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.llms.ollama import Ollama\n\n   llm = Ollama(\n       model=\"llama3.3\",\n       request_timeout=60.0,\n       context_window=8000,  # Adjust the context window as needed\n   )\n   ```\n\n   This is outlined in the context:  \n   \"Using a local LLM\" [llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/understanding/using_llms.md (lines 153-168)].\n\n2. **Set up the Hugging Face Embedding Model Globally**: Use the `HuggingFaceEmbedding` class from `llama_index.embeddings.huggingface`. This will ensure that any embedding operations use this model globally.\n\n   First, install the required package:\n   ```bash\n   pip install llama-index-embeddings-openai\n   ```\n\n   Then, configure the global embedding model in the `Settings` object:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.embeddings.openai import OpenAIEmbedding\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   Settings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding()\n   ```\n\n   This setup is described in the context under \"Usage Pattern\" [llama_index/docs/src/content/docs/framework/module_guides/models/embeddings.md (lines 15-62)].\n\nBy following these steps, LlamaIndex will use the specified local Ollama model and Hugging Face embedding model for all operations, ensuring that no external OpenAI services are contacted.",
